Problem Statement:  USC needs more reliable forms of transportation across campus 

 

Requirements: Bike/electric scooter lending service on campus 

Inputs: App that people put information in to keep people accountable for what they lend 

Output: The physical bike or scooter lent to the student: 

Specifications: It will be built to make sure people can reach their classes in time  

Ethics:  Would want to have tracking on the bikes to prevent them from being stolen which could cause concerns of tracking where students are going. (Would need User agreement) 

Evaluation:

   Functional 
     - Be able to properly lend out the bikes/scooters
     - Return process
     - User location to know where they could rent one 

   Nonfunctional 
     - App ease of use
     - Responsive and fast load times
     - Good UI and look 


Test Plan: 
  - Make sure the app can handle requests coming in at once like a stress test (Input would be sending in multiple requests. Output would be if the app can handle the requests and the speed of which it can)
  - Implement the system and get survey results about satisfaction with the service (Input is the users satisfaction. Output would be the results and what if they are good)
  - See if there is a change in the number of students late to class. (Input would be the amount of people late to class while the app is in use vs. when the app is not in use. Output would be if there was a change in the results)
  - Quality of the bike if it was in good condition (Input would be if the user reviewing the bikes condition and the output would be the results of if the bikes can be kept in a good condition)


Solution:
- Have an AI with location data of the user to reccomend the closest renting place
- User enters their information and picks up the bike
- When rental period ends notifies the user of the nearest drop off point to them
- If bike is not returned
 


 

